<title>USA: BPA offers no surplus power again for Thursday.</title>
<headline>BPA offers no surplus power again for Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bonneville Power Administration (BPA) did not offer any power for Thursday, the third consecutive day the agency has refrained from suprlus sales, it said Wednesday.</p>
<p>BPA said Tuesday it was purchasing power to cover generation being lost as several key reservoirs, including Grand Coulee in Washington, were being allowed to re-fill.</p>
<p>The lower discharge levels were expected to continue through Monday.</p>
<p>((--Los Angeles bureau, +1 213 955 6761))</p>
